        </div>
        <ul class="callout-list">
          <li><strong>The Price Gap:</strong> For the same $500,000 death benefit, whole life runs <strong>6 to 10 times more per month</strong> than a 20-year level term policy ($32/mo vs. $360/mo for a healthy 35-year-old).</li>
          <li><strong>High Drop-Off Rates:</strong> Society of Actuaries (SOA) studies show that over <strong>40% of whole life policies lapse or are surrendered within 10 years</strong>, locking in steep losses after upfront sales commissions and surrender fees.</li>
