      <p class="lead-text">
        No financial product sparks a sharper divide between salespeople and fee-only planners than life insurance. Commissioned agents pitch whole life as a "personal banking system" and tax-free wealth builder, while independent planners almost always point families toward plain term coverage. Look at the numbers behind both contracts and the reason becomes clear fast.
      </p>

